        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "refactor(ui): route Control UI pages through page modules",
        "body": "## What Problem This Solves\n\nThe Control UI routed every screen through one large render switch, coupling navigation, data loading, and page-specific lifecycle behavior. That made route isolation, lazy loading, and stale-data handling difficult to reason about and test.\n\n## Why This Change Was Made\n\nThis carries forward @shakkernerd's coherent router/page-module refactor, preserves the current Control UI shell and product behavior, and adds explicit route loaders, lifecycle hooks, loader dependencies, lazy page outlets, and route-level regression coverage. The later unfinished capability-host experiment from the source branch is intentionally excluded because it disabled most routes and did not pass the repository's type or test baselines.\n\n## User Impact\n\nNo intentional workflow change. Existing Control UI routes, navigation, responsive shell, chat sessions, agents, Workboard, cron, configuration, and mobile pairing continue to work while page ownership becomes isolated and lazy-loadable. Session-scoped Chat and Skill Workshop data now refresh correctly, including browser history navigation between Chat sessions.\n\n## Evidence\n\n- `OPENCLAW_VITEST_MAX_WORKERS=16 pnpm test ui/src` — 129 files, 1,727 tests passed\n- `OPENCLAW_VITEST_MAX_WORKERS=2 pnpm exec node scripts/test-projects.mjs test/vitest/vitest.unit-ui.config.ts` — 34 files, 835 tests passed\n- `pnpm test:ui:e2e` — 10 files, 31 tests passed\n- `pnpm lint --threads=8`\n- `pnpm check:architecture` — zero import cycles\n- `pnpm tsgo:core`\n- `pnpm tsgo:test:ui`\n- `pnpm --dir ui build`\n- `pnpm ui:i18n:check` — 20 locales clean, zero fallbacks\n- Fresh Codex autoreview after fixes — no accepted/actionable findings\n- Desktop, tablet, and mobile mock-Control-UI route renders inspected locally\n\nContributor history and authorship from @shakkernerd's `control-ui-refactor` branch are preserved in this branch.\n",
